 "title": "Early dense-eval loss as a cheap predictor of a FLOP-drop method's final 8k score",
 "result": "Partly. Train each method with its own forward, optimiser and real LR schedule for 10-50 steps from the repaired base on the same mt4 batches; score the DENSE forward's answer CE on fixed held-out 8k eval-rung rows (32/task, a probe, not a score). Steps 1-5 are uninformative (warmup + answer format: every arm 1.69 -> ~0.4). Step-10 / 20 CE vs the known final 8k mean over 19 arms x 2 seeds: Spearman 0.83 / 0.84 (0.82 / 0.85 with 16 rows/task; 0.75 / 0.83 on train-distribution rows). Step 20 separates every >=0.84 arm from every <0.80 arm except wtsS1 (outlier collapse invisible); step 10 also misses oracle 0.80. Both document-drop arms are flagged (excess +0.15 over dense LoRA at step 20, mostly contradiction). 30-50 steps (9 arms): Spearman 0.95; the step-50 outlier CE ranks outlier collapses at 0.97 (catches wtsS1). Limits: cannot resolve final gaps < ~0.03-0.05 (seed |diff| of the drop median 0.027, max 0.07; paired row SE ~0.013); nq / oolong carry no signal. Cost after a ~49 s load on 2 H200: ~51-54 s (10 steps), ~95 s (20), ~130 s (30), ~215 s (50) for recipe-like arms; oracle arms ~22 s/step.",
